Added the `[profile]` extra's PAS plugin (Gate 6b): member properties and user enumeration served entirely from Profile catalog brains, so a site can back its users with content objects and still answer "what is this user's full name" and "who matches 'liddell'" without loading a single Profile from the ZODB. That claim (C6) is now asserted rather than asserted-to-be-true: the tests patch `ZODB.Connection.setstate` and require the Profile load count to be zero while enumeration and property reads run, having first proved the objects were ghosts and the counter works. The plugin is installed above `mutable_properties`, so a Profile the user edited is what the site shows rather than the claim their provider sent at login — including when they deliberately cleared a field. Login names match regardless of case, at both ends: the index stores the folded form and every query folds. A Profile in the `deactivated` state stops being enumerated without being deleted, and which states count is a registry setting. `source_users` keeps enumerating alongside — PAS concatenates enumerators without deduplicating — and the two collapse back into one row because both return the same canonical userid, which the Sharing tab, `@users` and PlonePAS's search view all merge on. @ericof
